// The energy-to-HP rate of the game's damage model: how a round's line dose to a hard pool turns into
// HP points. Read by `src/ballistics/energy_dose.rs`, embedded and parsed once, validated at parse.
//
// A hard pool's line dose is the kinetic energy the round lost crossing it, ½ m (v_in² − v_out²),
// shared among the volumes present at each depth by their cost (chord × factor); a round
// that comes to rest inside it deals all it had left. One rate covers every hard pool, a tank's
// modules and a tree's trunk alike: a pool's authored HP alone says how sturdy it is. Crew are
// witnesses and keep their own law (the round's crew line rate, `wound` in `assets/rounds/`), and
// a field converts at its own calibration (`assets/ballistics/spall_cone.ron`). The law is design
// doc §6, `.agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md`.
//
// PROVENANCE: every value is authored `(value, Kind("source or reason"))`, Kind one of Measured,
// Derived, Tuned, Resolution, Unknown (`src/provenance.rs`); a value without one does not load.
(
    // Joules of energy lost per HP point. A box's line dose of E joules is E / this HP points, summed
    // with its other doses of the shot and rounded once.
    joules_per_hp: (3000.0, Tuned("provisional (issue 113): the pools authored under the
        reference-mm line law keep their scale for the main gun. That law charged 10 HP per
        reference-mm; the reference 88 mm APCBC round (10.2 kg, nose factor 7/24) at its 773 m/s
        muzzle speed loses about 3090 J per 0.1 mm of reference steel (DERIVED: the force law's
        A (a + k v²) × 1e-4 m, A = π/4 × 0.088² m², a = 3.711e9 Pa, k = 7/24 × 7850 kg/m³), rounded
        to 3000. A slower or smaller round deals less per reference-mm, a stopped one all it had
        left")),
)
